# ToolGuard git and Vercel

Standing instruction from the project owner. Follow it at the end of every coding task.

## Git

- Remote: `https://github.com/nhathung201/tool-guard-genlayer.git`
- Owner: `nhathung201/tool-guard-genlayer`
- Default branch: `main`
- When a requested coding task is finished, commit the relevant changes and push to `origin`.
- This standing request is the authorization to commit and push after coding work. Do not wait for a separate "commit" or "push" message.
- Do not force-push. Do not skip hooks. Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, keys).
- If there is nothing to commit, do not create an empty commit.

## Vercel

- Do not deploy, link, or push this project to Vercel.
- The owner deploys to Vercel themselves.
